---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Programmatic SEO + GEO Consulting",
  "serviceType": "Search Engine Optimization Consulting",
  "provider": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Pravine Manivannan", "url": "https://pravinemani.com/" },
  "areaServed": "Worldwide",
  "description": "Programmatic SEO, structured-data schema, GEO and AI-search visibility, and local SEO. Built on Next.js + Vercel with measurable indexation lift.",
  "url": "https://pravinemani.com/services/seo/"
};
---

<Base title="Programmatic SEO + GEO Consulting · Pravine Mani" description="Programmatic SEO, structured data, GEO and AI-search visibility, and local SEO. Built on Next.js + Vercel with measurable indexation lift. Toronto consultancy." jsonLd={jsonLd}>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/services/" style="color: var(--text-dim);">services</a>
    <span style="color: var(--text-muted, #444);">/</span>
    <span class="you">seo + geo</span>
  </div>
  <h1>Programmatic SEO + GEO,<br><span class="accent">engineered for AI search.</span></h1>
  <p class="lead">Search visibility built on Next.js and structured data, not WordPress plugins. Programmatic surfaces at scale, schema for every page type, and an llms.txt for AI-search crawlers. The redirect playbook preserves ranking authority through migrations.</p>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a href="/work/case-studies/cisnet/" class="cta-btn secondary">See the CISNET case study</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="vert-grid">

    <article class="vert-card" id="pseo">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">01</span><h2>Programmatic SEO</h2></div>
      <p>Hundreds of search-targeted pages generated from one content template plus your data: a page per city you serve, per product category, per use-case you solve. Each page is real, indexable and competes on its own.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>A written content model: which combinations earn a page, and which would be filler</li>
        <li>A working Next.js build that generates pages and the sitemap automatically as you add data</li>
        <li>Internal links between related pages so search authority flows where it should</li>
        <li>Safeguards so Google doesn't flag the pages as thin or low-value</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="schema">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">02</span><h2>Schema + structured data</h2></div>
      <p>Markup on each page that tells Google exactly what it is: a course, a business, an FAQ, a product. It earns the rich results in search (FAQ dropdowns, star ratings, business cards) and helps AI Overviews cite your content.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Rich-result eligibility for every page type your site has (Course, LocalBusiness, FAQ, Article, Product, and more)</li>
        <li>Breadcrumb navigation Google can read, which earns the "with breadcrumbs" lift in results</li>
        <li>FAQ and How-To markup added only on pages that can win featured snippets</li>
        <li>Every page validated through Google's Rich Results Test before it ships</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="geo">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">03</span><h2>GEO / AI search</h2></div>
      <p>Your site optimized to be cited by ChatGPT, Perplexity, Claude, Google AI Overviews and Bing Copilot, not just ranked in old-school search. The rules differ: pages need to be quotable in one sentence, not only rankable on a results page.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>An llms.txt file added to your site: robots.txt for AI crawlers, telling them what to read first</li>
        <li>Page content restructured so AI search engines can lift clean one-sentence answers</li>
        <li>Crawler permissions audited so the right AI tools reach your content and competitors can't scrape it</li>
        <li>Monthly tracking of which AI tools cite you and which cite your competitors instead</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="local">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">04</span><h2>Local SEO</h2></div>
      <p>For businesses serving a specific city, neighbourhood or service area. Show up in Google Maps, land in the local 3-pack, and keep reviews flowing. This is the maintenance work most agencies sell once and abandon.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Full Google Business Profile cleanup: categories, services, photos, hours and weekly posts</li>
        <li>Location pages that read like real content, not the doorway pages Google penalizes</li>
        <li>Directory cleanup across the citations that move local rank (Yelp, BBB, industry-specific)</li>
        <li>A review process that keeps your star count and review velocity healthy month over month</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="title-block">
      <div class="label">how it works</div>
      <h2>Engagement shapes for SEO work.</h2>
      <p>The same paid engagement shapes apply across every focus area. Full ladder at <a href="/services/">/services</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="vert-engagements">
    <a href="/services/#audit" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">SEO + GEO AUDIT</span><span class="when">FIXED-SCOPE WEEK · QUOTE ON SCOPE</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#sprint" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">PSEO SPRINT</span><span class="when">FIXED-SCOPE BUILD · QUOTE ON SCOPE</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#custom" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">SITE REBUILD</span><span class="when">MULTI-WORKFLOW · MILESTONE-PAID</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#retainer" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">OPS RETAINER</span><span class="when">MONTHLY · POST-ENGAGEMENT ONLY</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="vert-cta reveal" style="text-align: center;">
    <p style="margin: 0;">A migration or pSEO surface to scope? <a href="/contact/" style="color: var(--green); border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--green);">Send the brief →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

</Base>
